/ The home thread (design doc, sections 4 and 6). Every word of copy comes from
/ content/threads/home.yml. Without scripts it reads as a document: every strip
/ open, in order. With them the playback controller plays it, writing
/ data-state and data-open on each row (docs/system/home-thread-playback.md).
/ Each row's chart cell draws its piece of the git graph from the step's git
/ block. The filter controller, beside it on the wrapper, marks data-dim on the rows
/ of every controller but the one picked.
- content_for :title, @thread.page_title
- content_for :meta_description, @thread.description.truncate(155, separator: " ")
- content_for(:canonical_url) { root_url }

/ Playback hears the reader anywhere on the page: a wheel, a touch scroll, a
/ scroll key or a press on the scrollbar while it plays hands the page back (docs/rules/playback-yields.md).
div data-controller="playback filter" data-action="visibilitychange@document->playback#hide wheel@window->playback#scroll:passive touchmove@window->playback#scroll:passive pointerdown@window->playback#press keydown@window->playback#key"
  = render DockedBarComponent.new(steps: @thread.steps)
  main class="mx-auto max-w-page px-3 chart:px-8"
    / Stacked on a phone, scope first; side by side from 900 px.
    div class="flex flex-col gap-x-8 gap-y-4 pt-6 chart:flex-row chart:items-start"
      aside class="flex w-full max-w-column shrink-0 flex-col gap-2" aria-label="Scope and playback"
        = render ScopeComponent.new(steps: @thread.steps)
        = render StripBayComponent.new
        = render ControllerFilterComponent.new
        = render LegendComponent.new
      section class="min-w-0 flex-1 chart:pt-6"
        h1 class="text-headline"
          - if (link = @thread.headline_link)
            - before, text, after = @thread.headline.partition(link.text)
            = before
            = external_link_to text, link.url, class: "underline underline-offset-4"
            = after
          - else
            = @thread.headline
        p class="mt-4 max-w-measure" = @thread.intro
        div class="mt-6"
          = render LogComponent.new(steps: @thread.steps)

    section class="pt-4 pb-16" aria-labelledby="thread-heading" data-playback-target="thread"
      h2#thread-heading class="sr-only" The thread
      / The page keeps 96 px clear at its top (scroll-pt-16 on html), and
      / -scroll-mt-1 (-6 px) lifts each row so its strip, 6 px into it, lands
      / on that line when the page follows it or a link lands on it.
      - @thread.cells.each.with_index(1) do |cell, number|
        - step = cell.step
        div class="flex -scroll-mt-1" id=step.key style="--seconds: #{step.duration}" data-bay=step.bay data-lane=step.lane data-playback-target="row" data-filter-target="row"
          = render ChartCellComponent.new(cell:)
          div class="min-w-0 flex-1 py-1 pl-strip-gap"
            = render StripComponent.new(step:, number:)
            = render StepBodyComponent.new(step:)

  = render SiteFooterComponent.new do
    / What playback answers to from anywhere on the page but a text field
    / (docs/system/home-thread-playback.md, The keyboard).
    ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-3" aria-label="Keyboard" hidden=true data-playback-target="live"
      li
        kbd> Space
        | play or pause
      li
        kbd> j
        | next
      li
        kbd> k
        | previous
      li
        kbd> g
        | then
        kbd<> 1
        | –
        kbd<> = @thread.steps.count(&:gate?)
        | a gate
